AMASS Tool
•Amass is an open-source reconnaissance tool used for subdomain enumeration and attack surface mapping.
•It gathers information from DNS records, search engines, certificates, and public data sources.
•Helps security professionals discover hidden subdomains and network assets of a target domain.
•Supports both passive mode (no direct interaction) and active scanning.
•Commonly used in bug bounty, penetration testing, and OSINT reconnaissance.
•Can output results in multiple formats for further analysis.

Example command:
amass enum -d example.com
